        "original_id": "90c434f8-089c-5a98-8fcb-b65f2a438fe3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rihanna, Eminem, Destinee & Paris, Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Gwen Stefani\n- Songs: \"Love the Way You Lie (Part II)\", \"What's My Name?\", \"Only Girl (In the World)\", \"The Monster\", \"Love the Way You Lie\", \"Numb\"\n- Albums: Loud\n- Events: 2010 American Music Awards\n- Places: New Jersey, Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- In 2010, Rihanna released \"Only Girl (In the World)\" on her fifth album, Loud.\n- On November 21, 2010, Rihanna performed \"Love the Way You Lie (Part II)\" at the 2010 American Music Awards as part of a medley with \"What's My Name?\" and \"Only Girl (In the World)\".\n- \"Love the Way You Lie (Part II)\" received positive reviews from critics.\n- In 2012, \"Numb\" followed \"Love the Way You Lie\" and \"Love the Way You Lie (Part II)\" as collaborations between Eminem and Rihanna.\n- \"The Monster\" was the fourth collaboration between Eminem and Rihanna.\n- Destinee & Paris were born and raised in New Jersey and later became based in Los Angeles.\n- Destinee & Paris cited Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, and Gwen Stefani as influences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
